pourAddressT -- popups stroke 4b, B1 (SEQ 773, 2026-11-24; Tony's rulings of 2026-11-24, docs/popupsRecon.md section 6): THE
RETURN ADDRESS. Every poured row and cell is told, on the laid-out copy, where it came from; utilities' pourAddress(field)
answers for a clicked field "source S, entry E, member M", or "read-only: why", or "not poured". Nothing is written back
here (B2). Tester's shape; no window is shown; every click is a real mouse-up. A cell of a written row carries the fixture's
own click action and is handed to pourAddress itself; a derived row's cells cannot carry one, so there the selected field
is handed in. Each line also names the entry (of X).
Sources: PaThree (alpha beta gamma, colour values); PaWords (alpha only); PaActs (doIt, an action, and plain);
dESCRIPTIONs holds beta; fONTs and sTYLEs as they are.
A-1   WRITTEN ROW, {each.taG}: read-only, the entry's name.
A-2   {each}: source PaThree, entry beta (the second row), member value.
A-3   no text, fill:=each: the same address.
A-4   {PaWords.each}: source PaWords -- for alpha, which PaWords holds, and for beta, which it does not (the address names
      the entry all the same).
A-5   text holding an insert and more: read-only, computed.
A-6   text with no insert: read-only, written in the form.
A-7   the row itself, clicked past its last cell: read-only, a row holds no value.
A-8   an entry that is an action (doIt): read-only, and the action is NOT fired; its neighbour plain is writable.
A-9   DERIVED ROW (no template written): pourName read-only (the name); pourShow the entry's value in PaThree; pourWhat
      dESCRIPTIONs' entry of the name. Last click: the description cell of alpha, which has no description, so no text:
      it cannot be selected (only room), the selection climbs to the poured field, and that answers not poured. A cell
      that shows nothing cannot be reached by a click today.
A-10  derived from fONTs: pourShow is a font's sample text, read-only.
A-11  a field in no poured row: not poured.
A-12  derived from sTYLEs, a click down every row: some are a style's sample text and some a value read through the look,
      each read-only for that reason; none is writable. (Counted by reason: the rows are sTYLEs' own and may change.)
A-13  a pour inside a poured row: its cells are read-only, for that reason.
